\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  stocks jump 7% in biggest gain since 2009,  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  boosts real\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 21:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds closing prices, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, March 10 (Reuters) - Brazilian stocks chalked up their biggest one-day rise in 11 years on Tuesday, on growing hopes for global economic stimulus measures and as investors bought stocks battered down the previous day in the biggest selloff since 1998.\par \par \uc2 Shares in oil giant \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  and miner Vale led the rebound, rising 8.7% and 18.1%, respectively, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's third \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in two days helped drive the real's biggest rally this year.\par \par \uc2 A day after the real had slumped to a record low against the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2 billion on the spot market in the morning, bringing its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to $5.465 billion.\par \par \uc2 Local markets got a lift from the global relief rally, which saw Wall Street soar more than 4.5% as bargain hunting and hopes of government stimulus calmed investors' fears surrounding the coronavirus and growing signs of imminent recession.\par \par \uc2 "For those with a long-term investment horizon who weren't already invested (in stocks), this is an excellent time to buy shares," Rico Investimentos, a brokerage in Sao Paulo, said in a client note on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "For those already invested and with cash to take advantage of opportunities, the is also a very opportune time (to buy)," they added.\par \par \uc2 Preferred shares in state-controlled oil company \uc2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\uc2 , known as \uc2 Petrobras\uc2 , surged as much as 16% before easing back to close up 8.7%, and miner Vale SA's 18% rally was its biggest rise since January, 1999.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  shares sank 30%, their biggest ever one-day loss, which wiped almost 100 billion reais off its market value.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real rose 1.7% to close at 4.6457 per dollar , a day after slumping to an all-time low close to 4.80 per dollar. Some analysts said selling pressure on the real is likely to return soon, which will force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take even bolder action.\par \par \uc2 "Until now, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained discretion regarding these \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , announcing them on a daily basis at the expense of a medium-term \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan," Citi strategists wrote in a client note on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "With the escalation of the Covid-19 outbreak worldwide, the likelihood of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcing a \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan is increasing," they said. (Reporting by Jamie McGeever, Editing by Marguerita Choy and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-10T21:41:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200310eg3a02q5e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
