\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam assets crater after oil crash; coronavirus fears rise\b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 20:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Oil slides more than 30% \par     * Mexican peso set for its worst day in 3-1/2 years \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Colombia, Brazil, Chile hit record lows\par     * Brazil's Bovespa stock index drops as much as 10% \par     * Other stocks indexes in Latam slump between 3.6% and 10.5%\par \par  (Adds comments, updates price action)\par     By Shreyashi Sanyal and Susan Mathew\par     March 9 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso was set for its worst day\par in 3-1/2 years on Monday and Colombia's peso slumped to a record\par low as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of major oil exporters were hammered after\par crude lost a third of its value. \par     Oil prices fell as much as 30% after Saudi Arabia slashed\par its official crude selling price and set plans for a dramatic\par increase in production following Russia's refusal to help\par stabilize oil markets. The move shocked markets already reeling\par under pressure from the coronavirus outbreak.\par     "No one expected the Saudis to start a price war on oil, so\par to that extent it is a black swan event," said Max Gokhman, head\par of asset allocation at Pacific Life Fund Advisors in California.\par     "It creates a snowball effect where momentum just\par accelerates in whatever direction it was going. In this case it\par was down."\par     Brazil's real and the Chilean peso both sank \par to all-time lows. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will continue\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market using all tools at\par its disposal to whatever extent necessary to ensure the market\par functions smoothly.\par     Regional stocks plunged in line with a tumble on Wall\par Street, with Brazil's Bovespa stock index sinking 10%,\par triggering an automatic 15-minute halt. According to Eikon, the\par index has fallen 34.5% year to date, logging the steepest losses\par of any benchmark global index in dollar terms. \par     Preference shares of state oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  slid nearly 30% set for their worst day ever after\par the company cut diesel and gasoline prices following the slump\par in oil prices, a source said.\par     The oil shock comes as the fast-spreading coronavirus has\par been roiling markets for weeks, with the number of infected\par cases exceeding 110,000 worldwide leading to the suspension of \par economic activity and adding to fears of a global recession. \par     Colombian oil major \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped 17%, taking\par Colombia's main index down 8.7% - on track for its\par worst day since 2009, when the global financial crisis wreaked\par havoc across markets. \par     The moves took MSCI's index of emerging market stocks\par  down 6.1%, on track for its biggest percentage drop\par since 2011.\par     \par     OIL EXPORTERS BEAR THE BRUNT\par     The Mexican peso slipped as much as 8% to touch its\par lowest since early 2017. Several analysts now say that chances\par of an interest rate cut from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be\par shrinking at the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sinks to new lows.   \par     Colombia's peso was set for its worst day ever, down\par more than 6% to hit a new low of 3,835.\par     "There is likely to be a hit to growth in Mexico and\par Colombia. And weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in both countries will take\par interest rate cuts off the table, at least in the near-term,"\par said Quinn Markwith, emerging markets economist at Capital\par Economics. \par     A scurry to the safety of bonds and the Japanese yen\par quashed the dollar. Markets have fully priced in a\par 75-basis-point cut from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  later this\par month, hot on the heels of a 50-point cut emergency cut last\par week. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1845 GMT:\par     \par   Stock indexes            Latest        Daily %\par                                          change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets        950.01          -6.13\par                                       \par  MSCI LatAm                  1997.79         -12.69\par                                       \par  Brazil Bovespa             86507.54         -11.72\par                                       \par  Mexico IPC                 39009.47          -5.75\par                                       \par  Chile IPSA                  4060.21             -4\par                                       \par  Argentina MerVal           31201.64        -11.415\par                                       \par  Colombia COLCAP             1352.46         -10.01\par                                       \par                                                    \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest        Daily %\par                                          change\par  Brazil real                  4.7436          -2.32\par                                       \par  Mexico peso                 21.2310          -5.32\par                                       \par  Chile peso                    841.5          -1.82\par                       