\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Carnage in Latam as oil plummets; coronavirus fears rise\b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Oil slides more than 30% \par     * Mexican peso set for its worst day in 3-1/2 years \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Colombia, Brazil, Chile at record low\par     * Brazil's Bovespa stock index drops as much as 10% \par     * Other stocks indexes in Latam slump between 3.6% and 10.5%\par \par     By Susan Mathew\par     March 9 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso was set for its worst day\par in 3-1/2 years on Monday and Colombia's peso slumped to a record\par low as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of major crude oil exporters were hammered\par after oil lost a third of its value. \par     Oil prices fell as much as 30% after Saudi Arabia slashed\par its official crude selling price and set plans for a dramatic\par increase in production following Russia's refusal to help\par stabilize oil markets. The move shocked markets already reeling\par under pressure from the coronavirus outbreak.\par     Brazil's real and the Chilean peso both sank \par to all-time lows. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it will continue\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market using all tools at\par its disposal to whatever extent necessary to ensure the market\par functions smoothly.\par     Regional stocks plunged in line with a tumble on Wall\par Street, with Brazil's Bovespa stock index sinking 10%,\par triggering an automatic 15-minute halt. \par     Preference shares of state oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  crashed 24% in what could be their worst day ever\par after the company cut diesel and gasoline prices following the\par slump in oil prices, a source said.\par     "The oil price collapse adds a new dimension for fear and\par uncertainty," said David Bahnsen, chief investment officer at\par The Bahnsen Group. "Investors just have to brace for impact\par until more cards are on the table."   \par     The oil shock comes as the fast-spreading coronavirus has\par been roiling markets for weeks, with the number of infected\par cases exceeding 110,000 worldwide leading to the suspension of \par economic activity and adding to fears of a global recession. \par     Colombian oil major \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped 20%, taking\par Colombia's main index down 7.2% - on track for its\par worst day since 2009, when the global financial crisis wreaked\par havoc across markets. \par     The moves took MSCI's index of emerging market stocks\par  down 5.7%, on track for its biggest percentage drop\par since 2011.\par     \par     OIL EXPORTERS BEAR THE BRUNT\par     The Mexican peso slipped as much as 8% to touch its\par lowest since early 2017. Data showed Mexican consumer prices\par rose 3.70 percent in the year through February, further drifting\par above the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target rate. \par     "For the Mexican peso, it is also about completely unwinding\par the very heavy long positions that we've had build up over the\par last year," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christian Lawrence\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior market strategist at\par  Latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .  \par     While some analysts see Monday's decline as steep enough for\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hold rates steady next week, some\par say it may still cut, but by a more cautious 25 basis points,\par rather than 50 points expected as of last week.\par \par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will probably announce some\par options stabilization as in the past, but I don't think they\par will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot market."  \par     A scurry to the safety of bonds and the Japanese yen\par quashed the dollar. Markets have fully priced in a\par 75-basis-point cut from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  later this\par month, hot on the heels of a 50-point cut emergency cut last\par week.  \par     Colombia's peso was set for its worst day ever, down\par more than 6% to hit a new low of 3,835.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1449 GMT:\par    Stock indexes           Latest    Daily %\par                                      change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets       954.27    -5.71\par                                      \par  MSCI LatAm                 2057.87   -10.06\par                                      \par  Brazil Bovespa            89296.88    -8.88\par                                      \par  Mexico IPC                39667.35    -4.16\par                                      \par  Chile IPSA                 4076.68    -3.61\par                                      \par  Argentina MerVal          31518.59  -10.516\par                                      \par  Colombia COLCAP            1394.82    -7.19\par                                      \par                                             \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest    Daily %\par                                      change\par  Brazil real                 4.7400    -2.24\par                                      \par  Mexico peso                21.0960    -4.71\par                                      \par  Chile peso                   840.6    -1.71\par                                      \par  Colombia peso              3790.84    -5.45\par                                      \par  Peru sol                     3.498    -0.81\par                                      \par  Argentina peso             62.5200    -0.06\par  (interbank)                         \par                                      \par  \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; Editing by Dan\par Grebler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-9T16:27:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200309eg3902mww\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
