\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS- \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  pressure mounts on  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  to sell dollar reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 19:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, March 5 (Reuters) - Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weakening so quickly the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon be forced to set aside its free-market principles and sell dollar reserves to halt the slide.\par \par \uc2 Market volatility is rising, by some measures back to where it was when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last sold \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in November, and some analysts say the real's near-daily drops to new lows are now undermining confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Policymakers can reasonably say the real's 14% decline this year is a natural function of falling interest rates, that all emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are under heavy pressure and the selloff is not fueling inflation expectations in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Not that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sitting idly by. In recent weeks it sold some $6.5 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps market, where hedging demand from asset managers and investors is strongest.\par \par \uc2 But these actions have failed to slow the real's plunge, far less reverse it. The real weakened past 4.66 per dollar on Thursday, bringing its depreciation this week to 4%, one of its biggest weekly falls in years.\par \par \uc2 The previously unthinkable level of 5.00 per dollar is now on the horizon.\par \par \uc2 "I think they need to come with a program, perhaps announce a budget like $20 to $30 billion, either swaps or dollar reserves," said Carlos Kawall, director at Asa Bank in Sao Paulo. "They should announce that they are ready to do both."\par \par \uc2 Alexandre Song, portfolio manager at Macro Capital in Sao Paulo, warned that the longer the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lets the depreciation continue, the more traders will test its resolve and force it into an even greater policy response.\par \par \uc2 "It is clear that the small \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swaps market are not working, and the real's weakness is now becoming a self-fulfilling prophecy," Song said. "It's probably now time that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to start thinking of proper \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman told Reuters any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether in the derivatives or spot market, is determined by "market conditions."\par \par \uc2 VOLATILITY RISING\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  has said repeatedly this year that the real is a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , implying a reluctance to forcefully determine its path or level.\par \par \uc2 He and Bruno Serra, deputy governor for monetary policy and head of the bank's foreign reserves policy, are from trading backgrounds and firm believers in letting free markets determine asset prices. University of Chicago-educated Economy Minister Paulo Guedes is renowned for his laissez-faire economic views.\par \par \uc2 With Brazilian interest rates at a record low 4.25% \u8212\'20\'14 and likely to go even lower as the economic outlook dims \u8212\'20\'14 a weak exchange rate is simply "the new normal," according to Guedes.\par \par \uc2 Treasury Secretary Mansueto Almeida on Thursday said exchange rate policy is the sole responsibility of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding that the Treasury and the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  never take coordinated action on the real.\par \par \uc2 As reluctant as \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  and his colleagues might be to tap the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $360 billion stockpile of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the market might force their hand.\par \par \uc2 Implied three-month volatility on the dollar/real exchange rate rose to 12.5% on Thursday. That is higher than November, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last sold dollar reserves, and is closing in on the 14% in August, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unleashed its first dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 Tony Volpon, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at UBS in Sao Paulo and former \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director, said \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a limited resource that policymakers will only resort to when they feel they must.\par \par \uc2 "But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want to lose control of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has to keep an eye on financial stability," Volpon said. "They need to maintain an orderly \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jamie McGeever Editing by Brad Haynes and Steve Orlofsky) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-5T19:11:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200305eg3503oy5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
