\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real touches new low as Fed rate cut spurs bets of more easing\b0\par\par\uc2 517 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 20:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on Thursday \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GDP shows 2019 growth slowed, 2020 looks weak\par     * Mexico to speed up spending, spur private investment  \par \par  (Adds comment, updates throughout)\par     By Shreyashi Sanyal\par     March 4 (Reuters) - Brazil's real led a slide among Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday after an emergency interest\par rate cut from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  spurred expectations of\par more monetary easing in the region.    \par     The real slumped 1.3% to 4.5743 against the dollar\par , touching a fresh all-time low, while a rebounding\par greenback added to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's woes.    \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Latin America's biggest economy said it\par will auction up to $1 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps contracts\par on Thursday, the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid the real's\par more than 12% slide this year.\par     An emergency rate cut by the Fed on Tuesday to combat the\par economic impact from the fast-spreading coronavirus stoked fears\par that the extent of the fallout might be worse than anticipated\par and that regional central banks might follow suit. \par     "The Fed took center stage yesterday, offering the markets\par an unscripted 50bp cut. The reaction probably did not go as well\par as planned, as equities tanked in the aftermath," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mark\par McCormick\f28 \uc2 \f2 , global head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     "That said, the Fed's move has kick-started a new\par wave of easing."\par     Speculation is rife that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut\par interest rates by 25 basis points to a new low of 4%. \par     Data showed growth in Brazil's economy slowed last year with\par momentum pointing to a weak 2020, while a separate survey showed\par the country's dominant services sector expanded at its slowest\par pace in eight months in February.     \par     Mexico's plans to speed up public spending and is urging the\par private sector to boost investment to counter the impact of the\par coronavirus outbreak, Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Arturo Herrera\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on\par Tuesday, adding that the government was working closely with\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Mexico\f28 \uc2 \f2  to coordinate a suitable response. \par     Stocks in Brazil and Chile rallied\par strongly, in line with U.S. equities.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 IRB Brasil Resseguros\f28 \uc2 \f2  led losers on Sao Paulo's\par main index, plunging 34.5% after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Berkshire Hathaway\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par denied media reports that it was a shareholder in the Brazilian\par reinsurer.    \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1941 GMT:\par     \par   Stock indexes            Latest      Daily %\par                                         change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets       1036.76        0.87\p