\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real sinks to new low despite  \highlight22\uc2 central bank FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2020\par 18:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real fell to a fresh all-time low against the dollar on Friday, taking its losses so far this year to 11% as the relentless selling overwhelmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's third consecutive daily market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease the pressure.\par \par \uc2 As growing fears over the coronavirus outbreak slammed markets and investor sentiment around the world, Brazil's real brushed aside the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $1 billion sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps contracts to fall through 4.51 per dollar for the first time.\par \par \uc2 Traders said local investors sold the real as a hedge against their exposure to the Brazilian stock market, while local speculators also pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve.\par \par \uc2 The real traded as low as 4.5136 per dollar, and by mid-session in Brazil on Friday it had clawed back some ground to trade at 4.4950 reais per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "When the stock market is up and the economy is accelerating, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation is ignored. But when stocks sink and the economy cools down, a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes a big problem," said one senior trader in Sao Paulo. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now Brazil's main problem."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives market on Friday for the third time this week and fifth time this month, selling $1 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to slow the real's fall.\par \par \uc2 But if it had an effect, it was only to slow the decline. Economists note that with 2020 growth forecasts being revised down, in some cases below the politically-sensitive 2% threshold, it might be difficult for the real to bounce back meaningfully even when it does recover.\par \par \uc2 "The real was underperforming its emerging market peers even before concerns about (coronavirus) intensified in late January," wrote William Jackson at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  in a note on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We think a lot of this can be explained by Brazil's widening current account deficit, which will keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under pressure even if virus fears fade," he said. (Reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-28T18:04:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200228eg2s03m0l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
