\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real rebounds from record low; virus scare keeps stocks on edge\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2020\par 22:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Real firms over 1% as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sells dollars\par     * Brazilian equities fall on caution around coronavirus\par     * Other Latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mixed \par \par  (New throughout, updates prices, market activity and comments\par to close)\par     By Sruthi Shankar and Sagarika Jaisinghani\par     Feb 14 (Reuters) - Brazil's real rose on Friday and recorded\par its first weekly gain in seven, supported by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par move to stem a selloff in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while other Latin\par American assets came under pressure from concerns around the\par coronavirus epidemic.\par     The real firmed 1.26%, its biggest daily gain in two\par months, a day after as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $1 billion in\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps in its first market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par almost three months.  \par     Data showed economic activity in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell more than\par expected in December, tying in with other indicators that\par pointed to a slowdown in Latin America's largest economy at the\par end of last year.\par     The real, which was also battered in 2019 by failed oil\par auctions, has already lost more than 6% this year and is among\par the worst performing regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar.\par     "In the short-term, it (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) can certainly help\par the BRL, but it's hard to see a sustainable rally from the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alone," said Gordon Bowers, emerging markets fixed\par income analyst at Columbia Threadneedle.\par     "For the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to outperform, we need growth data to pick\par up."\par     The epidemic has prompted economists to cut growth forecasts\par for China's GDP in the first quarter and sparked a flight from\par assets in Brazil, among the main iron ore exporters to China.\par Brazilian equities fell 1.1% on Friday, sliding for the\par second straight session.\par     Health authorities reported about 5,000 new cases of the\par deadly virus on Friday, dashing earlier hopes that the outbreak\par was peaking. But global stock markets inched higher as\par policymakers pledged more monetary stimulus to limit its\par economic fallout.\par     The Mexican peso added about 0.2%, a day after\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexico's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its benchmark interest rate for a\par fifth consecutive time in the wake of a stagnating economy and\par slightly above-target headline inflation.\par     Colombia's peso slid 0.5%, while the Chilean peso\par  edged higher.\par        \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2113 GMT:\par  \par           Stock indexes                   Latest    Daily %\par                                                      change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                     1105.94     -0.01\par  MSCI LatAm                                2789.91     -0.13\par  Brazil Bovespa                          114378.62     -1.11\par  Mexico IPC                               44993.62     -0.03\par  Chile IPSA                                4655.86     -0.08\par  Argentina MerVal                         38647.68    -0.056\par  Colombia COLCAP                           1664.40      0.08\par                                                             \par              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                    Latest    Daily %\par                                                      change\par  Brazil real                                4.2934      1.31\par  Mexico peso                               18.5468      0.23\par  Chile peso                                  790.8      0.57\par  Colombia peso                             3390.61     -0.49\par  Peru sol                                    3.378      0.18\par  Argentina peso (interbank)                61.4575     -0.11\par                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Sruthi Shankar and Sagarika Jaisinghani in\par Bengaluru; Editing by David Gregorio)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-14T22:25:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200214eg2e03u49\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
