\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real jumps most since November as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  again\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2020\par 21:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates graphic)\par \par \uc2 By Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Brazil's real rose more than 1% against the dollar on Friday to chalk up its biggest rise since late November after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swaps market for the second straight day following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slump this week to new lows.\par \par \uc2 In late trading, the real was changing hands at 4.2940 per dollar, up 1.3% on the day. The greenback slid below 4.30 reais after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $1 billion sale of 20,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps contracts.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the greenback was at a record high above 4.38 reais before the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real was on course for a 0.5% rise on the week, snapping a run of six consecutive weekly declines that had brought its year-to-date losses against the dollar close to 10%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement "reaffirms expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would eventually try to cap the upside in dollar/real, and could bring some near-term support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Barclays\uc2  analysts wrote in a client note.\par \par \uc2 "However, we remain structurally bearish on the real, as disappointing growth, the erosion of carry, and a widening current account limits the attractiveness of Brazil as a destination for foreign portfolio flows," they added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered relief to those market participants bullish on the real, who had seen the exchange rate go against them. But traders said it may have to come back into the market if the real is to stage a more sustained recovery.\par \par \uc2 "$2 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps is nothing. They were able to curb the depreciation and make the real outperform, at least today. However, the framework is still very fragile," said one senior trader in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "With (market-based) rates going down and growth deteriorating, the market will try to buy dollars back," he said.\par \par \uc2 Citing weak economic growth, unattractive yields and a widening current account deficit, \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  on Friday revised their dollar/real outlook for this year to 4.50 from 4.25, one of the most bearish real forecasts among economists.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-14T21:03:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200214eg2e03ls9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
