\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real firms as c. bank sells dollars; shrugs off U.S. tariffs\b0\par\par\uc2 538 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2019\par 16:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Trump to restore tariffs on imports from Brazil, Argentina\par     * Brazil stocks rise 1% after strong manufacturing data\par     * Chilean peso firms as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kicks in\par \par     By Ambar Warrick\par     Dec 2 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real firmed on Monday as a spot\par auction by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following a\par tweet by U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  that said he was restoring\par tariffs on metal imports from Brazil and Argentina.\par     Without going into details, Trump said he would restore\par tariffs on U.S. steel and aluminum imports, surprising officials\par in the two South American countries and prompting them to seek\par explanations.\par     The real eased 0.4% immediately after the tweet, but\par reversed course after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold 9,600 reverse\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap contracts and $480 million in spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     The Argentine peso was largely unchanged, but the\par country's stock index fell about 1.7% after gaining for\par three days in a row. Aluminum producer Alua Aluminio Argentino\par  led declines on the index.\par     "We don't know what kind of response we're going to see\par (from Brazil and Argentina), but I suspect at this point it is\par more of a sell-the-news situation and then investors can settle\par back and interpret the data in a sober fashion," said Mark\par Luschini, chief investment strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janney Montgomery Scott\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par in Philadelphia.\par     A manufacturing rebound in China spurred optimism in Latin\par American markets, with the MSCI index tracking stocks in the\par region rising for the fourth straight session.\par \par     Brazilian stocks hit a near one-month high after\par data showed the country's manufacturing sector grew in November,\par pointing to a steady recovery in Latin America's largest\par economy.\par     Financials and material stocks were the biggest boosts to\par the Bovespa, while electronics retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Via Varejo SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par led gains after it flagged strong sales during the Black Friday\par discount shopping event.\par     Focus now turns to Brazil's third quarter economic growth\par data, due Tuesday, which is likely to show an expansion of 0.4%,\par according to a Reuters poll. \par     The Chilean peso firmed as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's $20\par billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program kicked in. The bank had\par outlined the plan last week after the peso hit a record low\par against the dollar. \par     The peso was also supported by higher prices for copper,\par Chile's largest export, as markets perceived increased demand\par for the metal following the stronger-than-expected Chinese data.\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1505 GMT:\par    \par      Stock indexes              Latest     Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets           1038.95              -0.11\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      2662.03               0.19\par                                         