\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile's peso jumps as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jolts shorts,  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real drops\b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2019\par 18:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Chile's peso sees second best day in 10 years on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real slides 1%, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's effect wanes\par \par     By Aaron Saldanha\par     Nov 29 (Reuters) - Chile's peso starred among Latin American\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday, bouncing off an all-time closing low on\par news of a chunky \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  program, which set it\par on course for its second best day in more than a decade.\par      The country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late on Thursday said it would\par sell up to $20 billion in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par starting on Monday aiming to stabilize the peso, which prompted\par some short-sellers to scale back bets on further weakness.\par  \par     "Chile has around $40 billion in reserves," said Guido\par Chamorro, a portfolio manager for Pictet Asset Management in\par London.\par     "This (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) program is $10 billion plus $10\par billion. It is a pretty big number but if it's big a number, it\par better work."     \par     The announcement had the desired effect despite the release\par of data on Friday showing manufacturing production\par dropped 5.8% in October from a year earlier, as well as news of\par sinking profit at state-owned copper mining giant Codelco.\par \par     Weekly Refinitiv Lipper data ended Nov. 20 showed\par international investors were still allocating money to a popular\par Chile-focused ETF despite increasingly violent protests\par against inequality which have led to over 25,000 people being\par detained.      \par     Simon Harvey, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market analyst at Monex Europe, said the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was "deemed credible" but he did not see the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firm to under the 800 peso-per-dollar mark due to local\par factors such as protests, instead suggesting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chilean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would allow the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken but at a slower pace\par than market factors dictate.    \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to have to strike the balance of\par cutting rates next week to stimulate growth while not making it\par counter-intuitive to their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets." \par     Moving in the other direction, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real weakened\par 1%, drifting towards a record low hit on Tuesday, as the effects\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wore off. \par     Monex Europe's Harvey said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real had traded in the 4\par to 4.20 reais-per-dollar range for most of the fourth quarter,\par which it had recently broken out of, leading to rising political\par pressure to bring it back within that range.\par     Nevertheless, the weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was providing some\par insulation to the local economy from slowing global growth and\par tepid external demand, he said.\par     Stocks on Sao Paulo's Bovespa dipped 0.4%, as the\par energy sector bore the brunt of a 2% decline in Brent crude\par futures, with shares of oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) falling 1%.\par     Mexican equities slid 0.5%, largely on losses among\par consumer staples and materials, broadly in line with the decline\par seen in the peso.\par     While Colombia's peso softened 0.5% and stocks\par  slipped 0.2%, Argentinean assets marked\par time. \par     \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1732 GMT:\par     \par      Stock indexes              Latest    Daily % change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets           1038.90           -1.09\par                                           \par  MSCI LatAm                      2646.39             0.1\par                                           \par  Brazil Bovespa                107911.41           -0.35\par                                           \par  Mexico IPC                     42872.20           -0.53\par                                           \par  Chile SPIPSA                    4515.26           -0.08\par                                           \par  Argentina MerVal               34264.79           0.132\par                                           \par  Colombia Colcap                 1600.71           -0.18\par                                           \par                                                         \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2               Latest    Daily % change\par  Brazil real                      4.2315           -0.38\par                                           \par  Mexico peso                     19.5520           -0.42\par                                           \par  Chile peso                        805.8            2.73\par                                           \par  Colombia peso                   3524.48           -0.38\par  Peru sol                          3.402           -0.24\par                                           \par  Argentina peso (interbank)      59.8500           -0.12\par                                           \par  \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Aaron Saldanha in Bengaluru, Additional reporting\par by Marc Jones in London; Editing by Lisa Shumaker)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-11-29T18:48:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020191129efbt02xmt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
