\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 IN MONEY / Brazil a "paper tiger"1\b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The litus-proof in the great crisis experienced today by south American countries is the case of Brazil, which is the largest economy in Latin America and on which many southern cone countries revolve.\par \par \uc2 The new Government of Bolsonaro has an ultra-neoliberal-trained cabinet that has externalized that the model to be followed is Chile's, just where this scheme failed.\par \par \uc2 In Chile, the social crisis is forcing a change of model, it wants to abandon extreme liberalism, to seek a greater welfare state.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Brazil's economy has serious structural problems:\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 Highly deficit public finances with accelerated growth in public debt.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 Dependence on exports of raw materials and markets such as China, Europe and Argentina.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 It's a very closed economy.\par \par \uc2 The state of public finances is extremely dangerous, according to \uc2 IMF\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 As a percentage of GDP, the primary deficit has been -0.6% in 2014, -1.9 in 2015, -2.5 in 2016, -1.8 in 2017, -1.7 in 2018 and -1.9 estimated for 2019.\par \par \uc2 The primary deficit is like cash flow, it is income without considering debt and spending, omitting debt service.\par \par \uc2 The worst thing in Brazil is the overall public deficit: -5.4% of GDP in 2014, -10.3 in 2015, -9 in 2016, -7.8 in 2017, -8.3 in 2018 and estimated the same as the latter for 2019.\par \par \uc2 This has detommed explosive growth in public debt, rising from 62.3% in 2014 to 78 in 2016 and to an \uc2 IMF\uc2  estimate of 92 in 2019.\par \par \uc2 The new government sold "the pearls of the virgin" seeking major reforms to heal public finances and undertake a process of trade opening that would make its economy competitive.\par \par \uc2 The reforms they would implement would be:\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 The pension system.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 A cut in wages and places to the bureaucracy.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 The extinguishing of public funds and the sale of government companies.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 Constitutional change to redefine the federation's departures to states.\par \par \uc2 So far the only thing that took place was pension reform, but its effects are year after year and within 10 will make a significant contribution to the consolidation of public finances.\par \par \uc2 The other reforms are stopped for several reasons:\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 Lack of strength in Congress by the Bolsonaro political group.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 Bureaucrats' opposition to privatizations, seater cuts and low-wages.\par \par \uc2 \u183\'00\'B7 Moderate success in \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  farm out.\par \par \uc2 Just on Tuesday, the Minister of economy declared that it was slowing down the remaining reforms because the conditions of social crisis in many countries, especially in Chile, which is its benchmark, made its discussion dangerous.\par \par \uc2 This is in addition to the disregard that your political group does not have sufficient consensus.\par \par \uc2 The "fiscal hole" in Brazil is very large, so it cannot afford to wait long; what has been profiled is that they will raise taxes to replace the income they should earn from reforms.\par \par \uc2 The effect has been a major depreciation of the exchange rate in recent weeks, but especially in recent days.\par \par \uc2 So far in November, the real has been devalued 6 percent and what follows.\par \par \uc2 The problem is that the crisis in Chile has widened in recent days, just yesterday the Chilean peso depreciated almost 3 percent, accumulating 15 percent since October 6 that the social crisis erupted, which I believe will end with a change of model.\par \par \uc2 So far the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to control parity. It should be remembered that he has $368 billion in reserves.\par \par \uc2 There's only little time and the "hole is big."\par \par \uc2 What does Mexico have to do with it?\par \par \uc2 As with Chile, the Mexican peso is used as a cover for Latam portfolios.\par \par \uc2 The price of the dollar in Mexico has risen 1.7% in November; although much less than the 10.56 from Brazil and 3.7 from Colombia.\par \par \uc2 joelmartinez132@gmail.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191128efbs000vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
