\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market again on Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2019\par 00:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with plans for Thursday market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; adds comment from Economy Ministry official)\par \par \uc2 By Jose Gomes Neto and Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Nov 27 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it will sell dollars on the spot market on Thursday, effectively its fourth bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week as the real has slumped to all-time lows.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will auction up to $1 billion in the spot market on Thursday, after the real finished trading at a record-low close of 4.26 per U.S. dollar on Wednesday. The bank this week already \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  once on Wednesday and twice on Tuesday, when the dollar reached a historic intraday low of nearly 4.28 reais.\par \par \uc2 The sale on Wednesday helped push the dollar back down to 4.2460 reais, but within 30 minutes of the auction it was already back up above 4.26 reais.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  on Tuesday evening said the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to fill liquidity gaps and because the market had become dysfunctional.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifted its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in August, when it sold dollars on the spot market without using additional instruments or a commitment to repurchase for the first time in a decade.\par \par \uc2 A senior Economy Ministry official told Reuters on Wednesday that the government's fiscal discipline and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's market expertise means there is little cause for concern.\par \par \uc2 "I'm relaxed about these movements," said Special Secretary Waldery Rodrigues, Economy Minister \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2 ' right-hand man. (Reporting by Jose Gomes Neto and Jamie McGeever Editing by Chizu Nomiyama and Leslie Adler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-11-28T00:25:51.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020191127efbr03j31\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
