\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Central raised the wholesale dollar by buying $140 million so as not to delay the peso against the real\b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Who would say that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would force the wholesale dollar to go up on a day when all the variants of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina dropped. It is that the 0.63% of the dollar in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the real, prompted the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make an effort and buy more dollars to raise the price and avoid delaying the exchange rate that is used for foreign trade.\par \par \uc2 Hence, of the US$368 million traded on the spot market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought 140 million and thus managed to get the wholesale dollar up to $59.97. The dollar until the last hour was at $62.70. The counterface was the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behavior at banks and exchanges where it dropped 4 cents to $62.87.\par \par \uc2 But what is happening in the wholesale market caused alternative dollars to fall sharply because big hands see a down-to-dollar fate because agribusiness is ahead of crop settlements. Those with dollars sell them through the settlement cash or the stock market dollar. There was so much supply that the "counted with liqui", as they call it in the jargon, dropped $1.77 (-2.4%) and the stock market dollar lost 82 cents at $70.11 (-1.2%). Of course, the offer made by triangulating bonds and stocks caused the prices of short- and medium-term government bonds and stocks to crumble. The free dollar had a day when it could celebrate a slight up 25 cents to $68.25.\par \par \uc2 The country's risk came back from 1.2 percent to 2,279 points from the New York-law dollar discount rise. This bond, with a high weighting in the j.P. Morgan index, has a parity that more than doubles those of the medium term, because investors find it difficult to enter default. That's why on Tuesday it rose 0.39% and helped country risk. It also helped keep the risk from skyrocketing, lowering the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Bond.\par \par \uc2 Source: RavaCentral Bank purchases raised reserves of USD 45 million to USD 43,736 million. The drop by lace was minimal, because on the benches the dripping was limited. What is known is that last Thursday the drop in deposits was only US$56 million, according to the latest information from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Stock Exchange suffered as a full mood from investors in the absence of data on the economic plan and poor balance sheets of companies. S&P Merval lost 4.1%. The only stock that went up was that of the Securities Market Group (VALO) with 0.98%. The rest had falls of up to 7.62% as was the case of Transportadora Gas del Sur. \uc2 Pampa Energ\u237\'00\'EDa\uc2  lost 5.99% and Central Port, 5.41%.\par \par \uc2 On Wall Street, Argentine ADRs - dollar-traded stockholding certificates - had mixed closures. For example IRSA Commercial Properties rose almost 24% and Take off, 7.39%. The strongest falls occurred in Transporter Gas del Sur (-7.52%) \uc2 BBVA\uc2  (-5.29%).\par \par \uc2 It is the rush to liquidate exports that dominates the market. Exporters influence the prices of bonds, stocks and alternative dollars. They have distrust in what's to come and are advancing export settlements.\par \par \uc2 I kept reading:\par \par \uc2 The dollar set a new record in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to relieve pressure on the real\par \par \uc2 What might be the consequences of not asking the \uc2 IMF\uc2  for more dollars, as Alberto Fernandez announced\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191127efbr001js\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
