\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The dollar set a new record in  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  and the  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened \highlight\uc2  to relieve pressure on the real\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to relieve the liquidity pressure on the real, which plummeted to an all-time low following comments from the minister of economy, \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2 , who claimed not to be concerned about weakness of the coin.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign auction of at least $1 million, shortly after President \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2  said he would like to see a dollar drop, pushed the green back more than two cents away from a new all-time high of 4.2689 re. Operators said it is unclear how much the bank finally auctioned.\par \par \uc2 "It's chaos," said the chief operating officer of a bank in Sao Paulo, referring to the swings that recorded the real price on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The record that hit the 4,289 reais dollar was about two cents higher than the previous peak reached in 2015, when Brazil became embroiled in one of the deepest and most painful recessions in its history.\par \par \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2  with Jair Bolsonaro (REUTERS/Ueslei Marcelino) (UESLEI MARCELINO/)Earlier on Tuesday, Bolsonaro said he would like the dollar to fall, but also endorsed the economy minister, Guedes, whose comments made on Monday were widely cited as the reason for the latest wave of sales.\par \par \uc2 "I saw that, and if that's what he said, it's said," Bolsonaro said in response to reporters' questions about Guedes' comments in Washington on Monday night and the subsequent fall of the real the next day. "I hope (the dollar) falls," he said.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to journalists in the US capital, Guedes said a weakened exchange rate is a natural consequence of falling interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "We have a floating coin, then it floats, " said Guedes. "When you have... lower interest rates, the equilibrium exchange rate is also higher," he said in reference to the dollar's versus real exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 (By Jamie McGeever - Reuters)\par \par \uc2 MORE ON THIS THEME:\par \par \uc2 Brazil's economy minister rekindled controversy by evoking the decree of the dictatorship that closed Congress\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191126efbq003zt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw181\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2715\pichgoal600
