\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank \highlight\uc2  to use most efficient  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  tools -director\b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2019\par 15:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, context)\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Sept 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use the most efficient tools at its disposal whenever it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the bank's director of monetary policy Bruno Serra Fernandes said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Debate around the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has intensified since it sold dollars in the spot market last month for the first time in over a decade, an indication it is willing to chip away at its $385 billion mountain of reserves.\par \par \uc2 In a presentation published on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website, Serra said the bank will use the "most efficient instruments at any given moment" when acting in the market, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps are an important tool when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not fully convertible.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  noted that in recent years hedging demand from investors and corporates meant it made sense to sell dollars via the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps market. But now, demand for dollars is building in the spot market as companies need hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay down foreign debt.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Serra said Brazilian firms are raising more cash on local capital markets, attracted by record low borrowing costs, which is allowing them to pay down debt overseas and "improving the Brazilian economy's net foreign liabilities."\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said on Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely watching the real's exchange rate for signs that its recent weakness is pushing up risk premia in financial markets or stoking inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 So far, neither appears to have happened, but the bank stands ready to take appropriate steps if it sees distortions in the market.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 4.16 reais) (Reporting by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Catherine Evans and Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-9-27T14:14:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190927ef9r0273a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
