\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  helps stabilize  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market, says  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's \uc2 Campos Neto\b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 September 2019\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, quote)\par \par \uc2 By Marcela Ayres and Jamie McGeever\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, Sept 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  serve to stabilize the market, Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Roberto Campos Neto\uc2  said on Thursday, in one of his first comments on the issue since the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's landmark \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is well-anchored and gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to cut interest rates again, while the underperforming economy should start to show solid signs of recovery later this year, \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said at an event in Brasilia.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2 's remarks on inflation and interest rates are consistent with his recent statements, while his remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first sale of dollars in the spot market in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  act as a mechanism of stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  said, adding Brazil's net reserves position was "pretty solid."\par \par \uc2 Last month, as the real slid toward 4.20 per dollar, its weakest level in almost a year and within sight of its record low around 4.25 per dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would sell dollars outright for the first time since 2009.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the real has bounced back to 4.07 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts said this marked a change of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is now much more willing to sell into its $385 billion pile of international reserves.\par \par \uc2 Campos Neto\uc2  also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a bill to simplify and lower the cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions in Brazil that was ready to put to lawmakers and should be voted on soon. The bill's ultimate aim will be full \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  convertibility within three to four years, he said.\par \par \uc2 On the current economic situation, growth has been weaker than expected, he said, but should start to pick up again later this year. Increasing the availability and reducing the cost of mortgage and infrastructure lending was one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top priorities, he said.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, low inflation provides space to further cut the benchmark Selic rate, currently at a record low 6.00%. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate-setting committee meets later this month and is widely expected to reduce the Selic again. (Reporting by Marcela Ayres Writing by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Bernadette Baum) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-9-5T14:46:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190905ef9502j4l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
