\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , stocks mostly weaker; Argentina peso jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2019\par 23:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Citi comments, updates prices)\par     By Susan Mathew\par     April 29 (Reuters) - Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened\par on Monday against a softer dollar, while the Argentine peso\par posted its biggest one-day gain in six months after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would ease limits on its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Mexico's peso and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's real both fell over\par 0.3%, while Chile's peso logged its ninth day of declines\par in ten as prices of copper - Chile's main export, fell.\par \par     Volatile oil prices took their toll on net crude exporter\par Colombia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which touched its lowest since early\par January. Peru's sol, however, climbed and had its best\par day in two months.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts have turned neutral from bullish on\par emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Some elements of our bullish view came together, such as a\par dovish \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a stabilization in China. Yet,\par EM has not picked up and new risks have come onto the horizon,"\par they wrote, pointing to fragile U.S.-Europe trade relations and\par rise in oil prices hurting crude importers as some key risks.\par     Argentina's troubled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soared 3.7%, and\par clocked its biggest intraday gain since early October as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision to ease limits on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signaled\par its willingness to sell reserves to better control the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's volatility.\par     This was previously not allowed under the country's $56\par billion standby financing deal with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary\par Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  and gives the bank more freedom to support the peso by\par loosening a no-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peso trading band that had been in\par place since October.\par     But analysts at Citi research expect Argentina to remain\par under pressure into early August, and warn of contagion from\par Latam's third largest economy.\par     As economic indicators showed deterioration, the peso -\par which lost half its value against the dollar last year -\par slumped, prompting Argentina to take measures to plug the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall. This has resulted in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seeing very\par volatile sessions recently.\par     Buenos Aires listed stocks slid nearly 4% on\par broad-based losses.\par     Other regional stock indices closed flat to lower. Brazil's\par Bovespa closed marginally lower as a near 6% jump in\par pharmaceutical firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hypera SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  was outweighed by\par losses among lenders.\par     Colombian stocks fell 0.4%, with shares of energy\par company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ecopetrol SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 0.5% as one of its pipelines\par was again bombed.\par     The country's Trasandino oil pipeline was bombed late on\par Friday, spilling crude into a nearby stream in the seventh time\par it has been attacked this year.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2100 GMT:\par     Stock indexes             Latest    Daily %\par                                          change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1082.91      0.45\par                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                    2761.63     -0.39\par                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa               96187.75     -0.05\par                                         \par  Mexico IPC                   44956.73     -0.04\par                                         \par  Chile IPSA                    5169.86     -0.42\par                                         \par  Argentina MerVal             28827.37     -3.91\par                                         \par  Colombia IGBC                12872.97     -0.38\par                                         \par                                                 \par        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              Latest    Daily %\par                                          change\par  Brazil real                    3.9442     -0.37\par                                         \par  Mexico peso                   19.0135    -0.343\par                                         \par  Chile peso                      679.5     -0.74\par                                         \par  Colombia peso                 3248.45     -0.67\par  Peru sol                         3.31      0.15\par                                         \par  Argentina peso                44.3500      3.61\par  (interbank)                            \par                                         \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; Editing by Richard\par Chang)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-4-29T22:14:58.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190429ef4t03sf7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
