\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL \highlight\uc2 : DI Rates Open Lower With USD After Renewed  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The one-day interbank deposit futures rates (DI rates) in Brazil opened lower Friday, influenced by the fall in the locally traded U.S. dollar, after a renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury to deter the greenback's appreciation. Investors also monitor the more hostile external environment amid escalating trade tensions abroad.Traders said that the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury have been trying to ease the market pressure by stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Thursday that it would keep the extra \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions, offering "around" US$ 10 billion next week.In the wake of this announcement, the Treasury said it would also make daily auctions to buy and sell pre-fixed (LTN and NTN-F) and post-fixed (NTN-B) bonds between June 18 and 22.\par \par \uc2  In addition, the National Monetary Council (CMN) changed the supplementary pension rule for the second time this year."These measures should have an impact in the short term, but the external scenario remains in focus and should have greater influence in the long term," says Renascen?a Corretora fixed income operator Luis Felipe Laudisio. He refers to the most challenging scenario for emerging countries and recalls that the intense movement in the U.S. dollar led to the pricing of a 1.50 percentage points (pp) increase in the Selic interest rate in 2018.For Icatu Vanguarda's market strategist, Dan Kawa, this pricing on the short end of the long curve impresses, amid a "very aggressive" cycle and starting at the next Monetary Policy Committee meeting next week.Near the middle of the session, the January 2019 DI contract rate was at 7.545%, from 7.60% in the previous session, while the January 2020 DI rate fell to 9.34%, from 9.37%. The January 2021 DI contract rate was at 10.33%, from 10.35%.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180615ee6f004pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
