\par\par \uc2 CENFENG\par \b \uc2 Without an official roof, the dollar took flight again and marked a new historic maximum\b0\par\par\uc2 822 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The peso yesterday ratified its comfortable leadership among the most devalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world against the American so far this year, closing at a new historical low. To the depreciation of the average 35.8% that had accumulated closed week 23 he added yesterday another drop of 2.7%, which almost doubled the fall in the same period had the Turkish lira (19%) and overcome in 2.4 times the one that suffered the real in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The data only confirm that, although the losses of value against the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are a global phenomenon related to the end of the era of the cheap dollar (which was opened as a result of the formula of resolution - with issuance of the subprime crisis), the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to be under attack even though the market is already wondering if this happens despite or precisely thanks to the recently announced with the (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The doubt is related to the conditions that the agency set for and the restrictions imposed on the (BCRA) to stop wasting reserves, which would aim to prompt a rapid correction of the bulging current account deficit through the exchange rate adjustment.\par \par \uc2 The concrete thing is that the new and abrupt jump of the dollar in the local square took place in a wheel of few businesses (only US $ 538 million were operated in cash) that had started quiet and that was complicated by the closure due to the marked reluctance of the sector private to sell dollars and the sustained pressure that maintains, despite the rise in prices, demand.\par \par \uc2 Until the last days that gap covered the public offer to try to dose the escalation. But yesterday the market had to operate without official positions (or the BCRA, now more limited, or the Nation, on behalf of the Treasury), which led to the price of the bill soared in minutes because "here nobody sells," noted the economist Fernando Camuso.\par \par \uc2 "The wholesale dollar had opened slightly offered with some aggressive sales of financial offer but then demand pressed and by not finding official offer or liquidations of exporters in quantity, boosted the price," said Agust\u237\'00\'EDn \u193\'00\'C1lvarez, of GLCapital.\par \par \uc2 "The banknote was operating at around $ 25.40 / 50 and suddenly the sellers disappeared, and it came to be seen in the system that offered to pay it at $ 26.50, but the maximum actually operated was $ 26.20," the broker explained in her report. ABC.\par \par \uc2 In this context, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed the day at an average of $ 25.99 and 26.10 for purchase and wholesale, with an increase of 79 cents (3.1%) from the level of $ 25.31 that had been on Friday. Following this trend, the retailer adjusted from $ 25.95 to $ 26.44 (+ 1.9%), according to the average that the BCRA reveals, by failing to capture the total correction that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had registered in large \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Until Thursday, the BCRA had maintained a mega-sale offer for up to 10% of its reserves at $ 25 to try to avoid further devaluation of the peso. According to its owner, \uc2 Federico Sturzenegger\uc2 , that value had been defined as a "frontier" because it was considered "out of scale", which reduced the chances that the market would challenge it. But once that offer disappeared, the devaluation pressure was again felt, despite the fact that interest rates remain at record nominal levels.\par \par \uc2 "This shows that the market did not see the $ 25 as an equilibrium price, which means that, for now, the flotation implies greater volatility and devaluation of the peso," even though, I suspect that if the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  had disappointed in amounts today we would be seeing the dollarwell above, "explained Martin Vauthier, economist director of the EcoGo Study.\par \par \uc2 "The agreement allowed us to encapsulate part of the punishment of Argentine peso and risk, but it does not uncouple us from emerging or regional risk, and we must keep in mind that the lira, the Mexican peso and the real are still down, despite the strong swap \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, "observed Erico Ritondale of EconViews.\par \par \uc2 "I think that beyond the agreement there is still some idea that the dollar is ' late & ' and that the government may not see with bad eyes let it rise this year a little more to have more room to delay it the next year, when there are elections, the $ 25 was evaluated as insufficient to correct the current account in the required magnitude ", says the economist Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Alfie, from Radar Consultora.\par \par \uc2 His colleague Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Hirch senses that the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  precisely caused the free dollar to be left as "a necessary hole for the economy to adjust what it has to adjust, by leaving the port open so that the pesos go to the dollar."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180719ee6d00bqx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
