\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  stocks rise after rout; real firms after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2018\par 20:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SAO PAULO, June 12 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's benchmark Bovespa\par equities index and real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  both rose\par moderately on Tuesday as traders saw room to take a breather\par amid a rocky stretch for Latin America's largest economy.\par     After an 8 percent fall in the Bovespa over the last five\par sessions, a slow news day at home combined with mixed political\par signals abroad resulted in limited buying opportunities.\par     Traders, however, warned that the rise was likely to be\par short-lived and was unsupported by fundamentals, with many\par bracing for cuts to Brazil's 2018 growth forecast for gross\par domestic product and with no moderate, market-friendly candidate\par gaining traction in the polls heading into the country's October\par presidential election.\par     "There's a clear absence of positive triggers for a buyers'\par recovery and an upward trend," said R\u233\'00\'E9gis Chinchila, an analyst\par at Rio de Janeiro-based Terra Investimentos.\par     The Bovespa climbed 0.5 percent in afternoon trade. \par     Among the biggest gainers were electronics retailers\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Magazine Luiza SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Via Varejo SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which\par climbed 3.3 percent and 6.8 percent, respectively, as it became\par clear that the long-term effects of an 11-day truckers' strike\par in late May would not be severe.\par     Shares of steelmakers \f28 \uc2 \f2 Usinas Siderurgicas de Minas Gerais SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cia Siderurgica Nacional SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose up\par 3.5 percent and 5.6 percent, respectively, as Brazil's president\par signed a decree loosening mining restrictions.\par     Brazil's real, which hit two-year lows in recent sessions\par before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market,\par climbed 0.53 percent against the dollar on Tuesday, trading at\par 3.70 to 1. That bucked a trend among major Latin American\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which generally fell on Tuesday amid expectations\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could signal two future interest rate\par hikes at its policy meeting this week.\par     Traders said the real was supported by the expectation that\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which said it would offer up to $20\par billion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps through the end of this week, would\par continue to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The market is still cautious because of the Fed meeting and\par due to domestic issues, but it remains measured with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  acting," said Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Carlos Amado, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at Sao\par Paulo brokerage Spinelli.  \par     The biggest loser among Latin American equities markets on\par Tuesday was Argentina's Merval index.\par     \par Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1736 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes               Latest      Daily    YTD pct\par                                           pct      change\par                                          change   \p