\par\par \b \uc2 Peso, Rand Join Emerging-Markets Slump; Is This Contagion? -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reshma Kapadia \par \uc2 673 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2018\par 20:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The turmoil in emerging markets has spread from Turkey and Argentina to wider held markets this week like \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline, a and in recent days to the Mexican peso and South African rand -- two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ending the week as the worst performers.\par \par \uc2 "The sense of contagion across higher-yielding markets is hard to ignore, "wrote \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  strategist Kit Juckes in his morning note.\par \par \uc2 But strategists aren't yet willing to yell "contagion" even as they grow more cautious. \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  's technical strategists noted that the MSCI Emerging Markets Index's weekly closes below the moving averages and its April and February lows put the recently bullish trend at risk and sets the stage for a retest of 2017 lows around 1100-1069. "Holding this support would make a case for a bullish breakout," they wrote. The MSCI Emerging Markets Index was last trading at 1149, down 0.49%.\par \par \uc2 Though emerging-markets fundamentals remain healthy, Luis Oganes, head of \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , commodities and emerging markets research, lowered his 2018 growth forecast by 0.2%, largely due to downward revisions in expectations for Latin America as Brazil and Argentina struggle. Though Asian emerging markets are expected to be more resilient, Oganes noted that China's economy could also dampen growth as trade tensions rise, China's sequential growth slows and external debt steadily rises.\par \par \uc2 BofAML emerging-markets strategist Ali Cakiroglu said benign inflation offers some cushion for emerging markets and he was finding select opportunities in equities as margins improve. But he perhaps summed it up best, saying the balance of risks was changing given all the moving parts.\par \par \uc2 Win Thin, BBH global head of emerging-markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, highlighted some of those moving parts in a note: Trade tensions are rising on this side of the Atlantic as Mexico retaliated against U.S. steel tariffs. Plus, India raised rates for the first time since 2014 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Urjit Patel\f28 \uc2 \f2   said it wasn't to defend the rupee and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signaled the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to defend its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Thin thinks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could start its own tightening cycle, raising rates by half a percentage point. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Oganes also highlighted the risk from emerging-market central banks, adding Indonesia and the Philippines to the countries that could be forced to tighten monetary policy to preserve financial stability. If tightening is "substantial," Oganes said it could lower medium-term growth and weigh down capital inflows in 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Outflows don't signal panic but do reflect angst. Over the last month, emerging-market equity exchange-traded funds saw $3.2 billion of outflows, coming in just second in terms of losers behind European Equity large-cap ETFs. The iShares Emerging Markets index ETF ( EEM) is down 0.48% over that period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When it comes to bonds, the Institute of International Finance wrote in a note this week, that fund outflows have been "characterized by a lack of selectivity, with both vulnerable and more insulated emerging markets hit by outflows from bond funds. That's unlike past periods of volatility, where selling was more targeted when China suffered a mini-devaluation in 2016 and after the election of President Donald Trump in 2016. The Wisdom Tree Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Strategy ETF (CEW) is down almost 4% over the last three months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That may be just the right conditions for picky money managers that my colleague Leslie P. Norton spoke to last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Varada Bhat contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sign up to Review & Preview, a new daily email from Barron's. Every evening we'll review the news that moved markets during the day and look ahead to what it means for your portfolio in the morning. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog,  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.barrons.com/emerging-markets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.barrons.com/emerging-markets }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 08, 2018 14:33 ET (18:33 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180608ee68002os\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
