\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. Dollar Rises Against Euro Ahead of \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  Meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ira Iosebashvili \par \uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2018\par 21:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose against the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday as investors braced for a \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  industrialized countries meeting this weekend where trade tensions are expected to dominate.\par \par \uc2 The euro was recently down 0.2% at $1.1770. The WSJ Dollar Index, which measures the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a basket of 16 others, was up 0.04% at 86.84.\par \par \uc2 In emerging markets, the dollar was recently down more than 5% against the Brazilian real. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to steady its falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to reports. The dollar has gained nearly 12% against the real this year.\par \par \uc2 "The markets viewed the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a credible measure," said Alvise Marino, a strategist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 In the longer term, fiscal pressures and political concerns likely to spur volatility in the real, he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ira Iosebashvili at ira.iosebashvili@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 08, 2018 15:55 ET (19:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180608ee680032r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
