\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  rebounds as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  calms markets\b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2018\par 15:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with market reaction, details of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , comments)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, June 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded sharply on Friday from a more than two-year low after \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Ilan Goldfajn\uc2  stepped up market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assured investors that the government had more measures at its disposal.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real gained more than 3 percent, erasing losses from the prior two days amid fears that more erratic policies and an unpredictable October election could set Brazil up for the next big emerging market rout.\par \par \uc2 Goldfajn reiterated in written comments on Friday a pledge he made at a Thursday night news conference to keep providing liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and interest rate markets as long as needed.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would offer up to $20 billion in new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps through the end of next week, picking up the pace after injecting the equivalent of $14 billion in futures markets since the middle of May.\par \par \uc2 "All instruments are valid," Goldfajn said, adding that "if there is demand, we may use reserves."\par \par \uc2 Interest futures also retreated from a recent spike, while the benchmark Bovespa stock index edged slightly higher.\par \par \uc2 Those comments appeared to staunch the real's bleeding, firming the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  3.4 percent to 3.793 reais to the U.S. dollar, after nearly hitting 4 reais to the dollar on Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Treasury will continue offering liquidity in a coordinated way, be it in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, be it in the interest rate market," Goldfajn said in talking points on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll showed the real is likely to strengthen in coming months but forecasts span an extremely wide range, highlighting how the recent slump has heightened uncertainty around the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. BRL/POLL (Reporting by Camila Moreira and Gram Slattery Editing by Brad Haynes, Frances Kerry and Bernadette Baum)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-6-11T13:53:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180608ee6800llt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
