\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil ETF On Track For Worst Day In More Than A Year As Country's Stock Exchange Faces A Rout -- \uc2 MarketWatch\b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2018\par 20:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 A popular exchange-traded fund used to track Brazil's equity market fell sharply on Thursday, coinciding with a sharp decline in the Brazil's main stock exchange. The \uc2 iShares MSCI Brazil ETF\uc2  (EWZ) was recently down 8%, putting it on track for its worst daily fall since May 18, 2017, according to FactSet data, while the BOVESPA Index was off 5.7%. The decline for Brazilian equities comes amid apprehension over recent labor unrest ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/economic-political-turbulence-hits-brazils-real-1528317886?mod=searchresults&page=1&pos=2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/economic-political-turbulence-hits-brazils-real-1528317886?mod=searchresults&page=1&pos=2}}}\uc2 ), with a strike of truckers, shaky economic growth and a presidential election slated for October. Reports on Thursday suggested that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  attempted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a selloff ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.zerohedge.com/news/2018-06-05/brazil-central-bank-intervention-fails-brl-rout-accelerates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.zerohedge.com/news/2018-06-05/\b  \highlight22brazil\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22central-bank\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 -fails-brl-rout-accelerates}}}\uc2 ) of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar , which was down about 2% against on the day and 4% thus far this week.\par \par \uc2  The Brazilian ETF, meanwhile, has lost more than 10% of its value so far this week and is on pace to shed 20% in 2018. By comparison, the S&P 500 index was up 3.5% so far this year, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average has returned about 2% in the first six months of the year.\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Mark DeCambre\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  For more from \f28 \uc2 \f2 MarketWatch\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/newsviewer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/newsviewer}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 07, 2018 14:32 ET (18:32 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180607ee67002sk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
