\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real plummets despite  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2018\par 16:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     BRASILIA, June 7 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real on Thursday\par plummeted to its weakest in more than two years, as concerns\par over the nation's fiscal outlook added fuel to a sell-off\par despite increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tumbled as much as 1.9 percent to 3.9132\par to the dollar, extending losses to  4.8 percent so far this\par month. It is down nearly 19 percent since February.\par     Rising U.S. bond yields have hit demand for emerging market\par assets in general, but Brazilian markets have been particularly\par affected after several opinion polls and a nationwide truckers'\par strike against high diesel prices cast doubt on bets that the\par winner of this year's elections will stick to a market-friendly\par agenda.\par     The sell-off drove the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to increase sales of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, which function like sales of dollars for future\par delivery, in a bid to cushion volatility.\par     Yet the real was still the biggest loser among Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , surpassing even the Mexican peso,\par which has been hard hit by fears that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 North American Free\par Trade Agreement\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 NAFTA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) negotiations may deteriorate.\par     A Reuters poll showed the real is likely to strengthen in\par coming months, but forecasts span an extremely wide range,\par highlighting how the recent slump has heightened uncertainty\par around the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate.\par     Assurances by central bankers that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sell-off\par will only drive monetary policy insofar as it affects inflation\par and inflation expectations also seemed to have little effect on\par markets, with yields on short-term interest rate futures\par  soaring.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  changed its plans and held rates at its\par last meeting because of the foreign outlook and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , so\par it's very reasonable that it could do so again for the same\par reasons," a partner at a Rio de Janeiro-based asset manager\par said, referring to the bank's unexpected decision to withhold\par from cutting rates last month.\par     Analysts told Reuters that the recent sell-off is unlikely\par to contaminate long-term inflation expectations, but that could\par change if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  breached the 4.00-to-the-dollar\par threshold.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1415 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                                daily %    YTD %\par                                      Latest    change   change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets               1150.02    -0.01    -0.71\par  MSCI LatAm                          2465.87    -2.03      -11\par  Brazil Bovespa                     74661.96    -1.91    -2.28\par  Mexico IPC                         45135.11     -0.1    -8.55\par  Chile IPSA                          5493.36    -0.07    -1.28\par  Chile IGPA                         27783.21    -0.05    -0.71\par  Argentina MerVal             