\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  weighed rate cut before opting to hold\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 2018\par 14:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds market reaction, details from minutes)\par \par \uc2 By Bruno Federowski and Marcela Ayres\par \par \uc2 BRASILIA, May 22 (Reuters) - \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considered cutting interest rates last week but ultimately left them untouched because of potential inflationary pressure stemming from a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the minutes of its most recent policy meeting showed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Last Wednesday, the bank unexpectedly kept the benchmark Selic rate at an all-time low of 6.50 percent, ending the deepest monetary easing cycle in a decade and defying widespread expectations of a 25-basis-point cut.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures fell in early trading as investors maintained bets that interest rates will stay low for a long time. Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real , strengthened in line with global emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The bank acknowledged that the decision came as a surprise to part of the market, giving policymakers reason to hesitate.\par \par \uc2 "Ultimately, an understanding prevailed that focusing on the best possible decision given the set of information available at the moment results, over time, in increased credibility for monetary policy," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 Inflation has remained below Brazil's official target range as a result of double-digit unemployment rates, widespread idle capacity and a slower-than-expected economic recovery, while year-end forecasts for 2018 and 2019 remain below the target's midpoint.\par \par \uc2 Yet the recent strength of the U.S. dollar, which drove the real to a two-year low, "reduced the likelihood that inflation will remain below the target in the foreseeable future through potential second-order effects on inflation," the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 Bets that a wider U.S. fiscal deficit and higher inflation could drive the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to increase rates by more than previously expected have pushed up U.S. bond yields, damping demand for emerging-market assets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to cushion the real's decline. The bank's minutes said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves will drive monetary policy only insofar as they affect the outlook for inflation.\par \par \uc2 A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushes up the cost of imports, although weak economic activity is likely to limit any pass-through to wider inflation. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will monitor several measures of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  effects on headline inflation and underlying price trends. (Reporting by Bruno Federowski and Marcela Ayres; Editing by Bernadette Baum and Steve Orlofsky) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-5-22T13:28:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180522ee5m00gqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
