\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil's real reverses slide after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  boosts swaps\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 2018\par 18:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SAO PAULO, May 21 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real rose almost\par 1 percent against the dollar on Monday, reversing a sharp slide\par in recent weeks, after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  boosted its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap program and said more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be on the\par way.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday evening said it would triple\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap contracts - equivalent to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sell\par dollars in futures markets - offered daily to 15,000, after the\par real fell to its lowest level in more than two years.\par \par     On Monday, the bank sold the 15,000 swaps and another set of\par 4,225 swaps.\par     By midday, the real had risen 0.83 percent to around\par 3.71 to the dollar, up from the Friday low of around 3.74 to the\par greenback. Traders said the real might have risen more had it\par not been for market caution ahead of the scheduled release on\par Tuesday of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes.\par     "The anticipation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes ... is making\par the market a little cautious," said Paulo Petrassi, a partner at\par Florianopolis, Brazil-based Leme Investimentos.\par     Argentina's volatile peso \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also gained on\par Monday, rising 0.95 percent against the dollar amid optimism\par over ongoing efforts by the government to obtain a financing\par line from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Consultancy Delphos Investimentos wrote in a note that there\par also appeared to be positive bias in the market regarding the\par possibility that index-provider MSCI might include the country\par in its emerging markets index, though the nation's Merval\par equities index fell on Monday amid profit-taking.\par     Last week, MSCI said Argentina's recent market turmoil would\par make more difficult a decision on elevating it from its current\par "frontier" market status. The decision is due next month.\par \par     Around the region, Latin America's equities markets were\par mixed, with Mexico's IPC index posting the only\par significant move, rising 0.6 percent as traders hunted for\par opportunities after the index hit its lowest point in 16 months\par on Friday.  \par     \par Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1520 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                           daily %     YTD %\par                              Latest       change    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets         1139.72      0.17     -1.79\par                                                   \par  MSCI LatAm                    2721.72      0.75     -4.48\par                                                   \par  Brazil Bovespa               82982.12     -0.12      8.61\par                                                   \par  Mexico IPC                   45938.75       0.6     -6.92\par                                                   \par  Chile IPSA                    5667.86     -0.38      1.86\par                                                   \par  Chile IGPA                   28