\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazilian real, Mexican peso dip amid selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2018\par 23:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     BRASILIA, May 18 (Reuters) - The Brazilian and Mexican\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened and stocks across Latin America fell on\par Friday as a global emerging-market selloff drove many investors\par to unwind bets on stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The real fell as much as 2 percent against the dollar\par to the weakest since March 2016, before recovering slightly to\par close 1 percent lower.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened for a sixth straight day, capping an\par 11.3 percent decline since the beginning of the year that made\par it the second-worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Latin America, behind\par only the Argentine peso.\par     Mexico's peso also fell more than 1 percent against\par the dollar as leaders in the United States and Mexico threw cold\par water on the prospect of a quick renegotiation of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 North\par American Free Trade Agreement\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 NAFTA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ). The peso and the\par benchmark Mexican stock index have now fallen for five\par weeks in a row.\par     Bets that a wider U.S. fiscal deficit and accelerating\par inflation could drive the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise interest\par rates more than expected have bumped up U.S. bond yields, luring\par capital away from higher-yielding emerging-market assets.\par     The selloff has extended for weeks, surprising many who were\par certain that the rout would fade quickly. A Reuters poll of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists earlier this month suggested Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would likely recoup much of their losses in\par coming months, though many warned of vulnerabilities in\par Argentina and Brazil.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness came even after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par increased market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and unexpectedly refrained from\par cutting interest rates this week.\par     The move highlights how emerging-market central banks have\par struggled to support their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The Argentine peso\par weakened around 1 percent on Thursday even as the country's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offered to sell additional dollars. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2100 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                                  daily %    YTD %\par                                                  change   change\par                                     Latest               \par  MSCI Emerging Markets                1137.75     -0.55    -1.79\par  MSCI LatAm                           2701.40     -1.89    -4.48\par  Brazil Bovespa                      83081.88     -0.65     8.74\par  Mexico IPC                          45666.77     -0.26    -7.47\par  Chile IPSA                           5667.86     -0.38     1.86\par  Chile IGPA                          28679.66     -0.29     2.50\par  Argentina MerVal                    31869.82       0.2   