\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real slumps despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  amid emerging market selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2018\par 16:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     BRASILIA, May 18 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real on Friday\par once again underperformed its Latin American peers as a global\par emerging market selloff drove many investors to unwind bets on a\par stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  despite increased \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The real weakened as much as 2 percent to 3.78 to the\par dollar, the weakest since March 2016, before paring back some of\par those gains to trade 1 percent lower.\par     It fell for a sixth straight day, capping an 11.3 percent\par decline since the beginning of the year that made it the\par second-worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Latin America, behind only\par the Argentine peso.\par     Bets that a wider U.S. fiscal deficit and accelerating\par inflation could drive the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise interest\par rates more than expected, have bumped up U.S. bond yields,\par luring capital away from higher-yielding, emerging-market\par assets.\par     The selloff has extended for weeks, surprising many who were\par certain that the rout would fade quickly. A Reuters poll of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists earlier this month suggested Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would likely recoup much of their losses in\par coming months, though many warned of vulnerabilities in\par Argentina and Brazil.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness came even after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par increased market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and unexpectedly refrained from\par cutting interest rates this week.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did the right thing by signaling concern\par with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness, but there's only so much you\par can do when you're dealing with a global repricing of the\par dollar," said a Rio de Janeiro-based portfolio manager.\par     "To some degree, you're also going to see increased daily\par volatility as traders test the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's willingness to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  even more."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has increased daily sales of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par swaps, which function like sales of dollars for future delivery.\par It holds $25 billion worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps in its books.\par     The move highlights how emerging-market central banks have\par struggled to support their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The Argentine peso\par weakened around 1 percent on Thursday even as the country's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  offered to sell additional dollars. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1350 GMT:\par  Stock indexes               