\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real up as c.bank resumes  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2017\par 23:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates with final prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, May 16 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real\par strengthened on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  resumed market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , providing support for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of a key\par vote on pension reform.\par     The Brazilian real firmed as much as 0.6 percent\par before paring gains to 0.34 percent as traders booked profit on\par a six-day stretch of gains.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $400 million worth of traditional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, which correspond to sales of dollars to\par investors for future delivery, to roll over June contracts.\par     Should it maintain that pace of sales daily throughout the\par end of May, as it has done in previous months, it will roll over\par all of the $4.4 billion worth of maturing swaps.\par     The move comes as the lower house of Congress prepares to\par vote on President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michel Temer\f28 \uc2 \f2 's flagship revamp of the Brazil's\par costly pension system, which investors say is needed to curtail\par growth of public debt and stave off recession.\par     Traders say the approval may trigger additional strength in\par the real, which has failed to rise consistently past 3.10 to the\par dollar since early February. Temer said on Monday a vote could\par take place by late May, though he still does not have the votes\par to pass it at this moment.\par     The real's move up also tracked strength in other Latin\par American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after weaker-than-expected U.S. housing\par figures supported expectations of a slower pace of interest rate\par increases in the country, potentially increasing appetite for\par riskier emerging-market assets.\par     Mexico's peso rose for a sixth straight session,\par closing up 0.3 percent at 18.65 per dollar.\par     Still, yields on Brazilian interest rate futures contracts\par  fell as traders bet the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could accelerate\par interest rate cuts this month to a brisk 1.25 percent basis\par points, taking the benchmark Selic rate to 10 percent.\par     Weaker-then-expected economic figures led economists at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco BTG Pactual SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  to forecast a 125 basis-point cut this\par month, followed by 100 basis-point and 75 basis-point reductions\par in July and September.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2150 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                           daily %    YTD %\par                                 Latest    change   change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets          1015.05     0.48    17.72\par                                                   \par  MSCI LatAm                     2761.44     0.36    17.98\par                                                   \par  Brazil Bovespa                68684.50     0.31    14.04\par                                                   \par  Mexico IPC                    49459.62    -0.44     8.36\par                                                   \par  Chile IPSA                     4875.40    -0.32    17.44\par                                                   \par  Chile IGPA                    24448.43    -0.26    17.91\par                          