\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real jumps on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2017\par 17:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SAO PAULO, April 17 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real jumped on\par Monday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , providing\par additional support for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid rising geopolitical\par frictions abroad and political concerns at home.\par     The real firmed 1.4 percent to the strongest in\par nearly two weeks after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $800 million worth\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, which function like dollar sales to investors\par for future delivery, to roll over contracts expiring next month.\par     Should the bank maintain that pace of sales daily until the\par end of the month, it will fully roll over $6.4 billion worth of\par swaps set to mature on March 2. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  currently holds\par around $17.7 billion worth of swaps on its balance sheet.\par     The move comes as escalating frictions between the United\par States and North Korea depressed investor appetite for\par high-yielding, emerging market assets. \par     U.S. Vice President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mike Pence\f28 \uc2 \f2  warned on Monday that recent\par U.S. military strikes in Syria and Afghanistan show that the\par resolve of President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  should not be tested, a day\par after a failed missile test by North Korea.\par     Demand for the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also wavered in recent\par days due to uncertainty over the approval of a planned pension\par reform following corruption investigations against senior\par members of President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michel Temer\f28 \uc2 \f2 's administration.\par     Other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seesawed on Monday as\par investors remained weary of the geopolitical tensions. The\par Mexican peso slipped from a five-month peak, but the\par Chilean peso followed copper prices higher.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1530 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                                daily %   YTD %\par                                                change  change\par                                    Latest              \par  MSCI Emerging Markets                962.33      0.2   11.38\par  MSCI LatAm                          2638.96     1.28   11.32\par  Brazil Bovespa                     63817.50     1.58    5.96\par  Mexico IPC                         49066.69     0.23    7.50\par  Chile IPSA                          4853.60     -0.1   16.92\par  Chile IGPA                         24343.38    -0.07   17.41\par  Argentina MerVal                   20753.58    -0.28   22.67\par  Colombia IGBC                      10162.69    -0.86    0.34\par  Venezuela IBC                      47196.37     0.35   48.86\par                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                    daily %   YTD %\par                                                change  change\par                                       Latest           \par  Brazil real                          3.1023     1.39    4.74\par  Mexico peso                         18.5600    -0.34   11.77\par  Chile peso                              646     0.64    3.82\par  Colombia peso                       2852.57     0.44    5.22\par  Peru sol                               3.25     0.12    5.05\par  Argentina peso (interbank)          15.2300    -0.26    4.24\par                                                        \par  Argentina peso (parallel)             15.76    -0.44    6.73\par                                                        \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski; Editing by Dan Grebler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-4-17T16:37:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170417ed4h00lrg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
