\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-LatAm  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  mostly weaken as U.S. inflation accelerates\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2017\par 15:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, Feb 15 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par mostly weakened on Wednesday after U.S. consumer prices rose by\par the most in nearly four years, fueling bets on higher U.S.\par interest rates.\par     The Labor Department said its Consumer Price Index jumped\par 0.6 percent last month, surpassing analyst expectations of a 0.3\par percent increase.\par     The figures came a day after U.S. Federal Reserve Chair\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  signaled rates could rise as soon as next month,\par despite uncertainty over President Donald Trump's policies.\par \par     The Mexican peso slipped 0.6 percent, while the\par Colombian peso weakened 0.4 percent.\par     The Brazilian real, however, firmed to the strongest\par in more than a year and a half, extending gains for a second day\par following a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision to resume \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's benchmark Bovespa stock index rose 0.8\par percent as expectations of higher U.S. rates lifted bank shares\par worldwide. Emerging market stocks had earlier hit a\par 19-month high.\par     Shares of Brazilian lender Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco SA rose\par 1.7 percent, adding the most points to the benchmark index.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco Bradesco SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  advanced 1.2 percent.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \