\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 , stocks post best year since 2009\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Dezember 2016\par 21:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Dec 29 (Reuters) - Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks closed 2016 with the best yearly performance in seven years, boosted by hopes that centre-right President \uc2 Michel Temer\uc2  would curb public spending following the ouster of his leftist predecessor \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real firmed 21.5 percent in 2016, breaking a five-year losing streak. It was by far the best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Latin America, and second only to the Russian rouble among emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Between 2011 and 2015, the real had lost more than half of its value as concerns over Brazil's ballooning public debt added to an emerging market rout.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index rose 38.9 percent in 2016 and advanced 68.8 percent in dollar terms, the world's best performing emerging market.\par \par \uc2 Shares in state-controlled firms led the gains, with oil company \uc2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leo Brasileiro SA\uc2  and lender \uc2 Banco do Brasil SA\uc2  doubling. Markets will be closed on Friday ahead of the New Year's Day holiday.\par \par \uc2 Whether the rally will continue hinges on Temer's ability to deliver fiscal and structural reforms amid corruption accusations encircling senior figures in his administration, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, doubts linger about U.S. President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's pledges of heavy infrastructure spending and tax cuts.\par \par \uc2 If the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  reacts by increasing rates faster than expected, that would likely weigh on demand for high-yielding Brazilian assets, according to Jason Vieira, chief economist at Infinity Asset Management Ltda.\par \par \uc2 "It's hard to decipher which of these forces will prevail," he said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters this month expected the real to weaken to 3.49 to the dollar in the next 12 months, from 3.25 currently. The estimates ranged between 2.98 and 3.88 reais, a sign of increased uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 Temer took over from Rousseff after she was impeached for allegedly meddling with fiscal accounts. He has pledged to reverse the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of her first term in a bid to end Brazil's deepest recession in decades.\par \par \uc2 Temer's government is likely to meet its target for the primary deficit - excluding debt payments - of 163.9 billion reais ($50.4 billion) in 2016, which it aims to cut to 143 billion reais next year.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, it forecasts gross debt to grow to 76.9 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) in 2017 from 70.5 percent in November.\par \par \uc2 Markets have cheered his administration's decision to impose a ceiling on growth in public spending, which was approved by Congress this month. He has also proposed reforms to the country's pension system, labor laws and tax code.\par \par \uc2 But corruption accusations against senior government figures, including Temer himself, could weaken the ruling coalition and derail reform efforts.\par \par \uc2 Volatility driven by the political newsflow, as well as Trump's unexpected victory, led \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It has stayed out of the market since Dec. 13 after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a near-daily basis since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 Many traders expect it to return to selling traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which function like selling future dollars, in order to smooth potential volatility early next year.\par \par \uc2 "It is likely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will roll over at least some of the swaps maturing in February," Cleber Alessie, a trader with H. Commcor DTVM Ltda brokerage, said.\par \par \uc2 "It is not in its interest to let them all expire and pressure the real given what is to come in 2017."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds $26.6 billion worth of swaps in its balance sheet, down from over $100 billion late last year. About $6.4 billion worth of swaps are set to expire on Feb. 1.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Claudia Violante and Bruno Federowski; Writing by Bruno Federowski; Editing by Bernadette Baum and Nick Zieminski) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-12-29T21:28:20.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161229ecct00zko\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
