\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken on strong U.S. economic data\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2016\par 02:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates with afternoon figures)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, Nov 23 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par weakened on Wednesday following strong U.S. economic figures,\par which hardened expectations of an interest rate increase by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  next month.\par     The Brazilian real closed down around 1 percent\par against the dollar, and the Mexican peso depreciated\par 0.27 percent against the greenback.\par     New orders of U.S. manufactured capital goods rebounded in\par October, while unemployment benefits rose last week, but\par remained consistent with a tightening labor market. \par     The figures reinforced expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par will increase rates in December, possibly draining capital away\par from high-yielding emerging markets.\par     Traders also purchased dollars ahead of Thanksgiving,\par seeking protection from unexpected market moves on Thursday and\par Friday.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not announce any market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for Wednesday after fully rolling over the $6.5\par billion worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps, which correspond to future\par dollar sales, maturing next month.\par     The bank had stepped up its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after U.S.\par President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's unexpected victory this month\par triggered an emerging market selloff.\par     Mexico's stock index closed up 0.7 percent after the\par country posted the fastest quarterly growth in over two years in\par the third quarter, official data showed. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2200 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                             daily %     YTD %\par                                Latest       change    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets            855.92     -0.18      7.78\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                      2301.11     -1.27     25.76\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                 61985.91      0.05     42.99\par                                                     \par  Mexico IPC                     45184.08       0.7      5.13\par                                                     \par  Chile IPSA                      4221.89      0.12     14.72\par                                                     \par  Chile IGPA                     21067.32      0.17     16.06\par                                                     \par  Argentina MerVal               17366.45      0.34     48.75\par                                                     \par  Colombia IGBC                   9717.87      0.21     13.69\par                                                     \par  Venezuela IBC                  25509.71      -2.6     74.86\par                                                     \par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                 daily %     YTD %\par                                             change    change\par                                   Latest            \par  Brazil real                      3