\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Assets Lose Ground Amid Concern Over Trump Policies -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2016\par 21:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 By Rogerio Jelmayer and Jeffrey T. Lewis\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real slumped and stocks fell Friday, joining other emerging markets as investors remain cautious about the impact \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's victory in the U.S. presidential election could have on the global economy.\par \par \uc2 A selloff that began in Asia rolled into markets in Europe, Africa and then Latin America through Friday's session.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real exited active trading at 3.4043, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. Brazil's benchmark stocks index, the Ibovespa, closed 3.3% lower. The real closed at 3.36 per dollar on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump could adopt a policy mix of increased fiscal spending on infrastructure projects and greater trade protectionism, some analysts said. This agenda could generate more inflation, leading, at some point, to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  raising interest rates more rapidly than previously expected, they said.\par \par \uc2 That in turn could lead to a shift in the dynamics that lured billions of dollars into emerging markets earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 If Mr. Trump follows through on trade policies he announced during the campaign, "the U.S. will become much more protectionist and hurt the global economy, including Brazil's," said Luiz Carlos Baldan, a director of the Fourtrade brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The real could even reach the BRL4.00 level in the next few weeks if the uncertainty persists, and if the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more actively, Mr. Baldan predicted.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. is \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second-most important trade partner after China, according to the South American country's trade ministry. Brazil posted a trade deficit of $847 million with the U.S. in the year through October, while Brazil reported a trade surplus of $11.45 billion with China in the same period.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in Friday to try to slow the dollar's gains against the real. The bank auctioned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts that have a similar effect to selling dollars, providing some support to the real.\par \par \uc2 The depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely prevent a more aggressive approach by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regarding the easing cycle of Selic base rate, according to some analysts.\par \par \uc2 In October, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its Selic benchmark interest rate to 14% from 14.25%, where it had been since July 2015, after inflation slowed. Some analysts said after that cut the bank was ready to assume an even more aggressive stance.\par \par \uc2 Cristiano Oliveira, chief economist at Banco Fibra, said he had been expecting a half-point cut at the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate meeting Nov. 30, but now he thinks the bank could opt for just a quarter point because of the real's recent performance against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Mario Mesquita, chief economist of Itau Unibanco, said he is now expecting a slower descent of the Selic.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are likely to remain skittish and choppy for several weeks, before some of the fog on President Trump's team and policy intentions are lifted," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Rogerio Jelmayer at rogerio.jelmayer@wsj.com and Jeffrey T. Lewis at Jeffrey.Lewis@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 11, 2016 15:56 ET (20:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161111ecbb0036t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
