\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real extends Trump-driven slump despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2016\par 20:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)               \par \par \uc2 By Bruno Federowski               \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real posted its worst three-day loss since 2008 on Friday even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid lingering concerns over the win of U.S. President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 The real weakened nearly 7 percent since Trump was elected on Tuesday.  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at its weakest since June, just shy of 1 percent lower on Friday at 3.3912 to the dollar.               \par \par \uc2 Trump's pledges of tax cuts and heavy public spending also fostered concerns that U.S. rates could rise more than expected in the coming months, draining capital away from high-yielding emerging markets.               \par \par \uc2 Yields on U.S. 30-year Treasury bonds rose 38 basis points on the week for its biggest weekly increase since January 2009, boosted by higher inflation expectations.               \par \par \uc2 Traders also fear a global trade shock if he makes good on promises to review U.S. trade accords.               \par \par \uc2 The sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move put \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on alert, driving it to suspend its daily auctions of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which function like dollar purchases by investors for future delivery.               \par \par \uc2 Early on Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold new traditional swaps in order to roll over the $6.5 billion contracts maturing next month, the first time it has done this since April. Investors often purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps in order to hedge against the possibility of a weaker real.               \par \par \uc2 Then in the afternoon, the bank offered two fresh lots of traditional swaps, not intended to roll over existing maturing positions, in an effort to counter volatility on the exchange market.               \par \par \uc2 The bank had used those contracts to reduce the amount of costly traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, equivalent to future dollar sales, on its balance sheet to $24 billion from over $100 billion late last year.               \par \par \uc2 "It shows that the current board is not dogmatic and has the ability to adapt to different market regimes," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  strategists said. "It goes in line with the goal of smoothing out \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  variations and containing excessive volatility."               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold all 15,000 swaps offered in the rollover auction, effectively injecting $750 million in additional market liquidity, leading the real to slightly pare losses to 3.41 per dollar.               \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the prospect of higher U.S. rates could also make the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  think twice before cutting rates sharply in the coming months.               \par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Ita\u250\'00\'FA Unibanco\uc2  now expect the bank to cut the benchmark Selic rate by 25 basis points in its November meeting from 50 basis points previously. Reuters calculations showed rate futures prices were consistent with a 25 basis point cut.               \par \par \uc2 The real has strengthened 15 percent so far this year, among the world's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as traders bet President \uc2 Michel Temer\uc2  would manage to rein in spending and curb debt growth.               \par \par \uc2 Concerns that Temer could face legal action over a donation from builder \uc2 Andrade Gutierrez\uc2  during the 2014 campaign of ousted President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2 , also weighed on the real. Temer was vice president under Rousseff.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-11-11T20:41:27.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161111ecbb00mun\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
