\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil financial inflows spike ahead of amnesty program deadline\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2016\par 19:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA/SAO PAULO, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Brazil saw nearly $1.6 billion in net financial inflows between Wednesday and Friday of last week, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said, as flows spiked ahead of the end-month expiry of an amnesty for the repatriation of irregular assets held abroad.\par \par \uc2 The head of economic research at \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tulio Maciel, told reporters on Tuesday that net financial inflows amounted to $740 million in the first 21 days of October as strong inflows at the end of the period offset sharp outflows in the beginning of the month.\par \par \uc2 The figure, which includes portfolio investment and FDI but excludes trade, compares to a $3 billion deficit in the same period of September.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has been bleeding capital for months as a deep recession and a sweeping corruption scandal dampened the allure of interest rates that are among the highest in the world.\par \par \uc2 Many traders had expected foreign investors to rush back to Brazil following the impeachment of leftist President \uc2 Dilma Rousseff\uc2  in May, but those inflows failed to materialize.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's largest economy saw almost $50 billion in financial outflows this year by Oct. 14, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts expect that trend to pause as Brazilians rush to beat the amnesty programme's Oct. 31 deadline.\par \par \uc2 The bill grants pardon to wealthy Brazilians holding undeclared assets abroad in exchange for a fine. The speaker of Brazil's lower house of Congress said last week the program is expected to collect 80 billion reais ($25.6 billion) in fines.\par \par \uc2 Assets declared under the amnesty do not necessarily have to be repatriated to Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Investor bets on strong inflows helped drive the real about 4 percent higher so far this month.\par \par \uc2 Late on Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would adjust its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy due to the "possibility of atypical flows of capital or excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  oscillations."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has about $30 billion reais in traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, contracts which function like dollar sales to investors for future delivery, on its books.\par \par \uc2 It has been reducing its exposure from over $100 billion late last year by selling on a daily basis reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, which work like future dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 But the bank said it will allow the $3.3 billion in traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps maturing on Nov. 1 to expire normally, instead of cancelling them in advance through reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps as it had done in the previous months.\par \par \uc2 This should offset strong inflows expected for Oct. 31, the last day of the repatriation program, traders said, as investors purchase dollars in the market to offset the maturing contracts. ($1 = 3.1201 reais) (Reporting by Marcela Ayres and Bruno Federowski; Editing by Daniel Flynn, Bernard Orr) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-10-25T18:25:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161025ecap00v6i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
