\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Goldfajn says to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market when needed\b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2016\par 16:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds Goldfajn comments and context)\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Aug 12 (Reuters) - Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Ilan Goldfajn reiterated on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cautiously use its tools when needed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened more than 1 percent earlier on Friday on comments from interim President \uc2 Michel Temer\uc2 , who told a local newspaper he is worried about the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Regarding the floating exchange rate, we have stated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at its discretion and without hurting the premises of this regime, will sparingly use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tools available," Goldfajn said at a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  event in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank will continue to reduce its traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps holdings without disrupting the market and depending on conditions.\par \par \uc2 By \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  constantly, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the volume of traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on its balance sheet from more than $100 billion last year to below $50 billion currently.\par \par \uc2 Goldfajn warned that high liquidity abroad and conditions that support moderate growth are not permanent and said the bank will remain cautious.\par \par \uc2 He reiterated that the bank will work to lower inflation to the 4.5 percent center of the official target in 2017. Twelve-month inflation currently stands at 8.74 percent on high food prices. (Reporting by Marcela Ayres; Writing by Alonso Soto; Editing by Jeffrey Benkoe) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-12T15:39:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160812ec8c00o0a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
